# Frontend stack (canonical)

Use these libraries for **all new frontend work**. Do not introduce alternatives.

| Concern | Library |
| --- | --- |
| UI primitives | **shadcn/ui** (`src/components/ui/`) |
| Auth security | **JWT + httpOnly cookies** (API issues/validates — see `plan.md` §7) |
| Auth FE UX | **Better Auth** (sign-in/up UI + client helpers on top of JWT+cookies) |
| Server/async state | **TanStack Query** (`@tanstack/react-query`) |
| Forms | **React Hook Form** + **Zod** (via `@hookform/resolvers`) |
| Client UI state | **Zustand** |
| Validation / schemas | **Zod** |

## Rules

- **Forms**: `useForm` + `FormProvider` + Zod (`zodResolver`) + `@/components/forms/fields`. Never use TanStack Form.
- **Data fetching**: TanStack Query only (`queryOptions`, `useSuspenseQuery` / `useQuery`, `useMutation`). No SWR, no ad-hoc `useEffect` + `fetch` for feature data.
- **Auth**: JWT + cookies are the real security model. Better Auth is FE UX only — do not treat it as a parallel auth backend. No Clerk. No access tokens in `localStorage`.
- **UI**: Extend or compose shadcn components; do not add parallel UI kits (MUI, Chakra, etc.).
- **Local state**: Zustand for cross-component client state; React state for local UI; nuqs for URL state (tables/filters).

## Legacy (do not expand)

- TanStack Form — removed; do not reintroduce.
- Clerk docs / cleanup templates — ignore for new features.
